{%- doc -%}
  "Request a combination" capture block for product pages. Renders an
  always-visible secondary button that opens a modal dialog offering up to
  three request paths, chosen with a radio group: (1) an out-of-stock
  combination, where the customer picks any option combination and sees a
  live availability status; (2) something different, a free-text description
  for anything outside the option matrix; and (3) a custom order, which hands
  off to a page chosen in the block's "Custom order page" setting (the radio
  and its panel render only when that setting points at a page). The selected
  path shows only its relevant fields;
  email is required on paths 1 and 2. Paths 1 and 2 send through Shopify's
  native contact form (full-page POST to /contact, guarded by Shopify's
  built-in spam protection); path 3 posts nothing, it is a link. Each form
  submission arrives as a structured email at the store's sender address.
  Inventory behavior is untouched.

  Conventions and caveats:

  - Marketing consent uses the paired-hidden-input encoding: a hidden
    `contact[Marketing consent]=No` sits immediately before the checkbox
    with value `Yes` and the same name; duplicate keys parse last-wins, so
    the merchant email always shows an explicit Yes or No. Consent is
    recorded as data only; nobody is auto-subscribed. No client-side
    timestamp field is included on purpose: it would be spoofable and the
    notification email's own Date header already captures when.
  - Option-derived field names carry a "Requested " prefix so a
    merchant-named option like "Email" or "Name" can never collide with
    Shopify's reserved contact keys; the fixed fields (Request type,
    Marketing consent, Product, Product URL, Availability) use static
    non-reserved names. Request type posts a fixed English token from the
    selected radio; Availability is "Not applicable" on the different path.
    Option names containing "[" or "]" would mangle under bracket-style
    param parsing; none exist on this store.
  - The customer-facing sold-out status means "variant exists but is not
    currently orderable". blocks/buy-buttons.liquid distinguishes Sold out
    from Unavailable more finely (inventory-policy aware); on this store
    (managed inventory, deny policy) the wordings coincide.
  - The hidden `contact[Availability]`, `contact[Product]`, and
    `contact[Product URL]` values are client-asserted hints that a direct
    POST can forge; treat them as triage aids, not facts, and do not click
    the URL reflexively on a suspicious submission.
  - There is no honeypot on purpose: Shopify processes /contact regardless
    of extra fields and nothing merchant-side can drop the email before the
    inbox, so the platform hCaptcha is the gate. The form carries
    data-shopify-captcha so that gate wires up even though the form is
    rendered inside a closed dialog; it still depends on the merchant keeping
    spam protection enabled (Online Store > Preferences).
  - Posted state (form.posted_successfully? / form.errors) is shared by
    every contact form on the page. Auto-reopening the dialog after the
    redirect is therefore gated on a sessionStorage snapshot written at
    submit time (see assets/request-combination.js). If the block is added
    twice on one template, both instances share posted state; the snapshot
    gate limits auto-reopen to the submitting product, and the first
    matching instance consumes the snapshot, so at most one dialog reopens.
    A snapshot written for a submission whose captcha challenge was
    abandoned persists for the tab session; the gate makes that cosmetic at
    worst.
  - The close button is first in the dialog DOM per
    docs/accessibility-patterns.md (Modal); blocks/popup-link.liquid places
    it last, which this block deliberately does not copy.
  - Renders nothing for products with only the default variant (no
    combinations to request) or outside a product context (except the theme
    editor's visual preview, which substitutes the first product).

  @example
  {% content_for 'block', type: 'request-combination', id: 'request-combination' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  if request.visual_preview_mode and product == blank
    assign product = collections.all.products.first
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank and product.has_only_default_variant == false -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign form_id = 'RequestCombination-' | append: block.id
    assign heading_id = 'RequestCombinationHeading-' | append: block.id
    assign email_error_id = 'RequestCombinationEmailError-' | append: block.id
    # The custom-order path and its radio render only when the merchant has
    # pointed the "Custom order page" setting at a page; leaving it blank
    # hides the option.
    assign custom_order_page = block.settings.custom_order_page
  -%}

  <request-combination-component
    class="request-combination spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block.settings %}"
    data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    data-status-available="{{ 'blocks.request_combination.status_available' | t }}"
    data-status-sold-out="{{ 'blocks.request_combination.status_sold_out' | t }}"
    data-status-not-offered="{{ 'blocks.request_combination.status_not_offered' | t }}"
    data-note-label="{{ 'blocks.request_combination.note_label' | t }}"
    data-description-label="{{ 'blocks.request_combination.description_label' | t }}"
    on:submit="/handleSubmit"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <button
      type="button"
      class="button button-secondary request-combination__trigger"
      aria-haspopup="dialog"
      on:click="/handleOpen"
    >
      {{- block.settings.button_label | escape -}}
    </button>

    <dialog
      ref="dialog"
      class="request-combination__dialog dialog-modal color-{{ settings.popover_color_scheme }}"
      aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}"
    >
      <button
        ref="closeButton"
        on:click="/closeDialog"
        class="button button-unstyled close-button request-combination__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close_dialog' | t }}"
      >
        {{- 'icon-close.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </button>

      <h2
        id="{{ heading_id }}"
        class="request-combination__heading"
      >
        {{- block.settings.heading | escape -}}
      </h2>

      {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
        <p class="request-combination__body">{{ block.settings.body | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Shopify auto-wires hCaptcha to contact forms present at page load, but
        this one is server-rendered inside a closed <dialog>; data-shopify-
        captcha forces immediate wiring so the hidden form is covered. Stays
        risk-based/invisible for real customers, and is inert if the merchant
        disables spam protection in Online Store > Preferences.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'contact', id: form_id, class: 'request-combination__form', return_to: product.url, data-shopify-captcha: 'true' -%}
        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <div
            id="{{ email_error_id }}"
            class="request-combination__error"
            ref="errorSummary"
            role="alert"
            tabindex="-1"
            autofocus
          >
            {{- 'icon-error.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            <span>
              {{- 'blocks.request_combination.error_heading' | t }}
              {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize | escape }}
              {{ form.errors.messages.email | escape -}}
            </span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <div
            class="request-combination__success"
            ref="successSummary"
            role="status"
            tabindex="-1"
            autofocus
          >
            {{- 'icon-checkmark.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
            <span>{{ 'blocks.request_combination.post_success' | t }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Request-type selector (two or three paths; the custom radio renders
          only when the custom-order page is set). The radio values are fixed
          English tokens (like the Availability tokens in the JS): they post to
          the merchant inbox as contact[Request type] and must not vary with
          the customer's storefront locale. Only the visible <span> labels are
          translated. "Stock" reveals the option selects + live status;
          "different" hides them (JS disables the selects so they don't post)
          and makes the note textarea a required description; "custom" hides the
          whole on-page form and shows the custom-order link.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <fieldset class="request-combination__paths">
          <legend>{{ 'blocks.request_combination.request_type_legend' | t }}</legend>
          <label class="request-combination__path">
            <input
              type="radio"
              name="contact[Request type]"
              value="Out of stock combination"
              data-path="stock"
              ref="pathRadios[]"
              on:change="/handlePathChange"
              checked
            >
            <span>{{ 'blocks.request_combination.request_type_stock' | t }}</span>
          </label>
          <label class="request-combination__path">
            <input
              type="radio"
              name="contact[Request type]"
              value="Different product version"
              data-path="different"
              ref="pathRadios[]"
              on:change="/handlePathChange"
            >
            <span>{{ 'blocks.request_combination.request_type_different' | t }}</span>
          </label>
          {%- if custom_order_page != blank -%}
            <label class="request-combination__path">
              <input
                type="radio"
                name="contact[Request type]"
                value="Custom order"
                data-path="custom"
                ref="pathRadios[]"
                on:change="/handlePathChange"
              >
              <span>{{ 'blocks.request_combination.request_type_custom' | t }}</span>
            </label>
          {%- endif -%}
        </fieldset>

        {%- comment -%}
          The on-page request form (email + path-specific fields + submit),
          shown for the stock and different paths. The custom path hides this
          whole block and shows the custom-order link below instead.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="request-combination__request-fields" ref="requestFields">
        {%- comment -%}
          Email sits directly under the path selector so its position is
          identical on the stock and different paths. Required on those two;
          disabled on the custom path, which posts nothing. The option selects
          and description below it swap in per the selected path.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="request-combination__field">
          <label for="RequestCombinationEmail-{{ block.id }}">
            {{- 'blocks.request_combination.email_label' | t -}}
            <span aria-hidden="true">*</span>
          </label>
          <input
            type="email"
            id="RequestCombinationEmail-{{ block.id }}"
            class="request-combination__input"
            autocomplete="email"
            name="contact[email]"
            ref="emailField"
            spellcheck="false"
            autocapitalize="off"
            value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email | escape }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email | escape }}{% endif %}"
            required
            aria-required="true"
            {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}
              aria-invalid="true"
              aria-describedby="{{ email_error_id }}"
            {% endif %}
          >
        </div>

        <div class="request-combination__stock-fields" ref="stockFields">
        {%- for product_option in product.options_with_values -%}
          <div class="request-combination__field">
            <label for="RequestCombinationOption-{{ block.id }}-{{ forloop.index0 }}">
              {{- product_option.name | escape -}}
            </label>
            <select
              id="RequestCombinationOption-{{ block.id }}-{{ forloop.index0 }}"
              class="request-combination__input"
              name="contact[Requested {{ product_option.name | escape }}]"
              ref="optionSelects[]"
              on:change="/handleOptionChange"
            >
              {%- for product_option_value in product_option.values -%}
                <option
                  value="{{ product_option_value | escape }}"
                  {% if product_option_value.selected %}
                    selected
                  {% endif %}
                >
                  {{- product_option_value | escape -}}
                </option>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </select>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Populated by JS at dialog-open time. The dialog is unreachable
          without JS, so no server-rendered status text is needed.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p
          ref="statusLine"
          class="request-combination__status"
          role="status"
          hidden
        ></p>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Shared note/description textarea. In the "stock" path it is an
          optional note; in the "different" path JS swaps the label to the
          description copy, reveals the required marker, and toggles the
          required / aria-required attributes so the browser enforces a
          non-empty description. One contact[body] field keeps the merchant
          email consistent across the stock and different paths.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="request-combination__field">
          <label for="RequestCombinationNote-{{ block.id }}">
            <span ref="noteLabelText">{{ 'blocks.request_combination.note_label' | t }}</span>
            <span ref="noteRequiredMark" aria-hidden="true" hidden>*</span>
          </label>
          <textarea
            rows="3"
            id="RequestCombinationNote-{{ block.id }}"
            class="request-combination__input request-combination__input--textarea"
            name="contact[body]"
            ref="noteField"
            aria-required="false"
          >{{- form.body | escape -}}</textarea>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Paired-hidden-input consent encoding: the hidden No must sit
          immediately before the same-named Yes checkbox (last-wins). See the
          doc block above before changing either input.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <input
          type="hidden"
          name="contact[Marketing consent]"
          value="No"
        >
        {%- liquid
          # The t filter HTML-escapes its output, so this single pass is
          # already safe for snippets/checkbox.liquid, which renders its label
          # param raw (data-label attribute + span text). Do not add | escape:
          # it double-escapes and renders entities like &#39; literally.
          assign consent_label_text = 'blocks.request_combination.consent_label' | t
          assign consent_id = 'RequestCombinationConsent-' | append: block.id
        -%}
        {% render 'checkbox',
          name: 'contact[Marketing consent]',
          value: 'Yes',
          label: consent_label_text,
          id: consent_id,
          checked: false,
          events: '',
          disabled: false
        %}

        <input
          type="hidden"
          name="contact[Product]"
          value="{{ product.title | escape }}"
        >
        <input
          type="hidden"
          name="contact[Product URL]"
          value="{{ shop.url | append: product.url | escape }}"
        >
        <input
          type="hidden"
          name="contact[Availability]"
          ref="availabilityField"
          value="Not verified"
        >

        <button
          type="submit"
          class="button request-combination__submit"
        >
          {{- 'blocks.request_combination.submit_label' | t -}}
        </button>
        </div>

        {%- if custom_order_page != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Custom path hands off to the dedicated custom-orders page. This is
            a link, not a form submission: nothing posts from this path.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div
            class="request-combination__custom"
            ref="customFields"
            hidden
          >
            <p class="request-combination__custom-text">
              {{- 'blocks.request_combination.custom_blurb' | t -}}
            </p>
            <a
              href="{{ custom_order_page.url }}"
              class="button request-combination__custom-link"
            >
              {{- 'blocks.request_combination.custom_cta' | t -}}
            </a>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Reduced availability map for the live status line. Fields are pinned
        to exactly options + available: never add inventory_quantity,
        inventory_policy, or SKU here (this JSON is public page content).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <script
        type="application/json"
        ref="variantData"
      >
        [
          {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
            {"options": {{ variant.options | json }}, "available": {{ variant.available | json }}}
            {%- unless forloop.last %},{% endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      </script>
    </dialog>
  </request-combination-component>

  <script
    src="{{ 'request-combination.js' | asset_url }}"
    type="module"
    fetchpriority="low"
  ></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .request-combination {
    display: block;
  }

  .request-combination__trigger {
    inline-size: 100%;
    min-block-size: var(--minimum-touch-target);
  }

  /* Hide the trigger until the component upgrades, so a no-JS or
     pre-hydration page never shows an inert button (the dialog needs JS to
     open). */
  request-combination-component:not(:defined) .request-combination__trigger {
    display: none;
  }

  .request-combination__dialog {
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-popover);
    border: var(--style-border-popover);
    border-radius: var(--style-border-radius-popover);
    background-color: var(--color-background);
    padding: var(--padding-4xl) var(--padding-xl) var(--padding-xl);
    inline-size: min(30rem, calc(100vw - var(--padding-xl) * 2));
    max-block-size: var(--modal-max-height);
    overflow-y: auto;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding: var(--padding-5xl);
    }
  }

  .request-combination__dialog[open] {
    animation: modalSlideInTop var(--animation-speed) var(--animation-easing) forwards;
  }

  .request-combination__dialog.dialog-closing {
    animation: modalSlideOutTop var(--animation-speed) var(--animation-easing) forwards;
  }

  /* Explicit position so placement anchors to the dialog rather than
     silently depending on the slide-in animation's terminal transform. */
  .request-combination__close {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--margin-2xs);
    right: var(--margin-2xs);
    opacity: 0.8;
    animation: none;
  }

  .request-combination__heading {
    margin-block: 0 var(--margin-sm);
    font-size: var(--font-size--2xl);
  }

  .request-combination__body {
    margin-block: 0 var(--margin-md);
  }

  .request-combination__form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--gap-md);
  }

  .request-combination__field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--gap-2xs);
  }

  .request-combination__paths {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--gap-2xs);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .request-combination__paths legend {
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-end: var(--gap-2xs);
    font-size: var(--font-size--sm);
  }

  /* Bordered option rows so the choices read as one group and match the
     bordered selects / inputs below them. */
  .request-combination__path {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--gap-xs);
    min-block-size: var(--minimum-touch-target);
    padding-inline: var(--padding-xl);
    border: var(--style-border-width-inputs) solid var(--color-input-border);
    border-radius: var(--style-border-radius-inputs);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .request-combination__path:has(input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--color-input-text);
  }

  .request-combination__stock-fields {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--gap-md);
  }

  .request-combination__stock-fields[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .request-combination__request-fields,
  .request-combination__custom {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--gap-md);
  }

  .request-combination__request-fields[hidden],
  .request-combination__custom[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .request-combination__custom-text {
    margin-block: 0;
  }

  .request-combination__custom-link {
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  .request-combination__input {
    inline-size: 100%;
    color: var(--color-input-text);
    background-color: var(--color-input-background);
    padding: var(--padding-lg) var(--padding-xl);
    border-radius: var(--style-border-radius-inputs);
    border: var(--style-border-width-inputs) solid var(--color-input-border);
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  .request-combination__input--textarea {
    resize: vertical;
  }

  .request-combination__status {
    margin-block: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size--sm);
  }

  .request-combination__error,
  .request-combination__success {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--gap-xs);
  }

  /*
   * The shared checkbox snippet (snippets/checkbox.liquid) ships with
   * white-space: nowrap + text-overflow: ellipsis on .checkbox__label-text
   * (assets/base.css) because it was designed for short labels. The consent
   * copy is a full sentence; allow wrapping here only. Same override as
   * blocks/return-policy-acknowledgment.liquid, documented there.
   */
  .request-combination .checkbox__label {
    align-items: flex-start;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .request-combination .checkbox__label-text {
    white-space: normal;
    overflow: visible;
    text-overflow: clip;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.request_combination",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "button_label",
      "label": "t:settings.request_combination.button_label",
      "default": "t:settings.request_combination.button_label_default"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "t:settings.request_combination.heading",
      "default": "t:settings.request_combination.heading_default"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "t:settings.request_combination.body",
      "default": "t:settings.request_combination.body_default"
    },
    {
      "type": "page",
      "id": "custom_order_page",
      "label": "t:settings.request_combination.custom_order_page",
      "info": "t:settings.request_combination.custom_order_page_info"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:content.padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "t:settings.top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "t:settings.bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-inline-start", "label": "t:settings.left", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-inline-end", "label": "t:settings.right", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "t:names.request_combination", "category": "t:categories.product" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
